solution.p:
To solve, we first separate the variable terms and constant terms to different sides of the equation. Then we eliminate the variable terms coefficient.
\begin{aligned}
7-3y\amp=-8\\
7-3y\subtractright{7}\amp=-8\subtractright{7}\\
-3y\amp=-15\\
\divideunder{-3y}{-3}\amp=\divideunder{-15}{-3}\\
y\amp=5
\end{aligned}
Checking the solution y=5\text{:}
\begin{aligned}
7-3y\amp=-8\\
7-3(\substitute{5})\amp\wonder{=}-8\\
7-15\amp\confirm{=}-8
\end{aligned}
So the solution to the equation 7-3y=-8 is 5 and the solution set is \{5\}\text{.}
